  "result": "`Cart.remove('sku-1')` now removes the Widget line. All 7 tests pass, and the demo prints `1`, meaning only the Gadget line is left.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/models.py:31`, `Cart.remove` filtered lines by `l.item.name != sku` instead of `l.item.sku`. The demo compared `'sku-1'` to the name `'Widget'`, found no match, and removed nothing. Removal only worked when an item's name happened to be the same as its SKU. The existing tests didn't catch this because they never call `remove`.\n\n**Fix:** that line now compares `l.item.sku != sku`, which matches how `Cart.add` finds lines.\n\nI also added a regression test, `test_remove_by_sku`, to `tests/test_pricing.py`. It recreates the demo cart and checks that only `sku-2` remains.\n\nThis machine has no `python` command, so I ran everything with `python3 -m unittest -v` and `python3 -m shop.demo`.",
